+## Routes
+
+- `POST /import/sales` takes `{ "csv": "..." }` with columns
+  `ticket,soldAt,dishId,qty`. `soldAt` is an ISO instant with a timezone; `qty`
+  is a positive whole number of portions. Returns `{ "tickets": 2, "dishes": 5 }`
+  counting newly imported tickets and total portions. Previously imported tickets
+  are skipped. Every row is validated; any invalid row or stock shortage rejects
+  the entire file with a `sales_row` error naming its physical CSV row.
+- `GET /reports/variance?from=YYYY-MM-DD&to=YYYY-MM-DD` returns an array of
+  `{ "itemId": 1, "theoretical": 2, "actual": 3, "variance": 1 }`, sorted by
+  item id. Days are inclusive and in UTC; `from` must not follow `to`.
+  Theoretical use is the ingredient quantities saved at sale import; actual use
+  includes every consume movement. Variance is actual minus theoretical, in the
+  item's unit. Items with neither use are omitted.
