+## Sales (schema 3)
+
+Schema 2 migrates to schema 3 by adding an empty `sales` collection and
+`seq.sale`. Each sale row has an id, ticket, soldAt (normalized UTC instant),
+dishId, qty (portions), and a snapshot of scaled ingredient quantities.
+Tickets are deduplicated across imports, while multiple rows in a new ticket
+are all imported. The whole file commits atomically, including ids and ledger
+movements. Sale consumption uses `sale:<ticket>` as its ledger reference and
+`soldAt` as its movement time. Historical theory uses saved ingredients.
